ed by Joatham, as they had been by his father, chap. xxvi. 7."],["haydock",7,null,"haydock","Wars, with Rasin and Phacee, 4 Kings xv. 37. — Juda. What concerned both kingdoms was carefully preserved; and Esdras informs us from what records he composed this work. (Calmet)"]],"au":{"haydock":["George Leo Haydock",0,0,1849,"https://www.newadvent.org/cathen/07160a.htm"]}}